Patch 0009. One correction that matters legally, and the artefact that wins the
follow-on engagement.

FIX — A QUOTATION MUST NEVER REACH THE REPOSITORY

`cost add` wrote to the bundled, version-controlled library by default. That is
wrong twice over: a fabricated price would raise the evidence class of a real
study, and a genuine supplier quotation is confidential and frequently under NDA,
so it must never be committed or shipped in an image. Now there are two files and
the distinction is enforced:

  gridforge/data/cost_library.json   committed seed — placeholders and published
                                     benchmarks only, figures anyone may read
  cost_library.local.json            yours — gitignored, never in the image,
                                     overlaid on the seed at runtime

`cost add` writes privately by default and REFUSES to put a quotation in the seed.
A quotation without --supplier and --quoted-on is rejected outright: without them
it is not a quotation, it is a number someone remembered. `cost where` shows which
files are in play, and a test plus a CI step fail the build if a quotation ever
appears in the committed seed.

THE WALKTHROUGH DECK (gridforge/reporting/deck.py, POST /v1/deck)

    python3 -m gridforge deck intake.json -o out

Nine slides from the same solved model as the written study, so slide and report
can never disagree — a walkthrough that contradicts the deliverable is worse than
no walkthrough. Arrow keys to advance; a print stylesheet turns each slide into one
landscape page, so Print to PDF produces something sendable. No network, no fonts
to fetch, no script from anywhere: a client can open it on a plane. A test asserts
there is no URL in the output.

It ships automatically with a purchased Envelope Study and appears on the client's
deliverable page beside the document; a failed deck never fails the document,
because the document is what was bought. The Screen does not include one.

Two charts, and the colour work is deliberate. #00E5FF and #FFB020 are interface
colours; as data marks against the panel surface they sit outside the usable
lightness band. The deck uses dimmed steps of the same hues, validated for
lightness, chroma, colour-vision separation and contrast, and every value a mark
encodes is also printed — nothing is knowable by colour alone. The energisation
curve keeps one point per distinct week: several ladder steps routinely complete in
the same week, and stacking a column of dots on one x position reads as noise and
implies events the client will never experience.

137 Python tests pass, up from 127. tsc, next lint and next build clean.
Migration 0004 adds deck_html to deliverables.

